    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d138">

                <pb facs="0182" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114A/251</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-18T11:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 18, 1918, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 3.36 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. [From Garrett]:</p>
                <p>Commission desires to insert the following article in proposed agreement:
                    “Officer prisoners of war shall be paid in advance as soon as possible after
                    capture for the remainder [of the current] month and thereafter on the first day
                    of each calendar month.”</p>
                <p>In view of the fact that such payments are to be reimbursed to the captor state,
                    commission requests to be instructed as to whether its adoption would violate
                    any existing statute. Garrett.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
